{"/api/discogs/artist/10019749/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"10019749","image":"https://i.discogs.com/1QFnFLw0aEawpMtmg05n_P3I922G4Gi6LjXkbdtv2_g/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:411/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwMDE5/NzQ5LTE2NDg2NDEx/MTAtNzUwNi5wbmc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/rOPUYEWXLt30EA9SzssyQqCSyqw7D-wEC5BrQHIyndw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEwMDE5/NzQ5LTE2NDg2NDEx/MTAtNzUwNi5wbmc.jpeg","profile":"Looking for personal ways of working with the physicality of bass through sound systems, Notte Infinita is pursuing emotional narratives through sound gestures and textures. Notte Infinita is inspired by spaces, dreams and meditative/euphoric states","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:10019749","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/10019749-Notte-Infinita","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/notteinfinita","https://www.instagram.com/notteinfinita/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/1166342/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1166342","image":"https://i.discogs.com/bzhOSy0rNsvP4P8ZxQxMSEvzpFl3ztz4eVDhtk3Cb_0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:500/w:500/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTExNjYz/NDItMTQ3NjMwNzUy/My0xMDM4LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/hINSih9SG03QJ-MInTNgwI9Ipw3NBPTckMCyM-QYaM4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTExNjYz/NDItMTQ3NjMwNzUy/My0xMDM4LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1166342","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1166342-The-Clerk","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.facebook.com/theclerkmusic/","https://soundcloud.com/the_clerk"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/1233462/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1233462","image":"https://i.discogs.com/AIKRgzbaggA1rn2re5zNHdENsuWa47oqG3e3pjSXdcQ/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEyMzM0/NjItMTUxODIxMjk5/My02MDIxLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/X-EKYVifiUKxFbqrsJJzQke8Ob2qemEDHOtU_V3lHx4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTEyMzM0/NjItMTUxODIxMjk5/My02MDIxLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Dutch-Surinamese hip-hop performer and DJ, born May 11th, 1985 in Amersfoort, Utrecht, the Netherlands, performing with lyrics in English and Dutch.\r\n\r\nBorn in Amersfoort, his father was a record store owner (Radio Roelandschap), Bizzey founded the group [a=Yellow Claw], together with Jim Aasgier and Nizzle in 2010, before leaving the group and focusing on a solo career in 2016.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:1233462","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":1233848,"name":"Leo Roelandschap"},{"id":16728241,"name":"Leyo (4)"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["MC Bizzey"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/1233462-Bizzey","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.bizzey.nl","https://www.facebook.com/bizzeybrooks/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/22061/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"22061","image":"https://i.discogs.com/n2Zu3I4q4vP-HX3eYQ78DeR3tZreWtxw-edKv-g3Zl4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:419/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIyMDYx/LTE2MzExNDg1NDct/NTI4My5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/dmtr2_T96CZuH0YmIxua2eoI-jPJWuW49Z8sLWoQU_k/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIyMDYx/LTE2MzExNDg1NDct/NTI4My5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Japanese electropop band, formed in 1978.\r\n\r\nThe principal members are Haruomi Hosono (bass), Yukihiro Takahashi (drums) and Ryuichi Sakamoto (keyboards).\r\n\r\nThe band was originally conceived as a one-off studio project by Hosono, the other two members being recruited session musicians - the idea was to produce an album fusing orientalist exotica (cf their cover version of Martin Denny's Firecracker) with modern electronics. However the first album (with its cutting-edge production) was very popular, and the studio project grew into a fully fledged touring band and career for its three members.\r\n\r\nMaking abundant use of new synthesizers, samplers, digital and computer recording technology as it became available, their popularity and influence extended beyond Japan. Generally the band are highly regarded as pioneers of electronic music, and continue to be remixed and sampled by modern artists.\r\n\r\nThe band had stopped working together by 1984 (deliberately using a Japanese term meaning \"spreading out\" or \"branching out\" rather than saying they were \"splitting up\"); the three members returning to their solo careers but continuing to collaborate. They released a one-off reunion album, Technodon, in 1993.\r\n\r\nThe early 2000s saw Hosono & Takahashi reunited in a project called Sketch Show. On a number of occasions Ryuichi Sakamoto has joined in on Sketch Show performances and recording sessions. He later proposed they rename the unit \"Human Audio Sponge\" when he participates, although outside Japan they also used \"Yellow Magic Orchestra\" until ownership issues with former label Alfa were resolved, so subsequent live releases use the original band name. \r\n\r\nOricon chart statistics - \r\nSingles:\r\nTechnopolis : 9 in Oricon chart, 293,000 copies sold\r\nRydeen: 15 in Oricon chart, 225,000 copies sold\r\nTighten Up: 43 in Oricon chart, 38,000 copies sold\r\nKimi Ni Mune Kyun: 2 in Oricon chart, 347,000 copies sold\r\nKageki Na Shukujo: 15 in Oricon chart, 79,000 copies sold\r\nIshin Denshin: 23 on Oricon chart, 57,000 copies sold\r\n\r\nAlbums:\r\nYellow Magic Orchestra (US Mix): 20 on Oricon chart, 250,000 copies sold\r\nSolid State Survivor: 1 on Oricon chart, 1,021,000 copies sold\r\nPublic Pressure: 1 on Oricon chart, 393,000 copies sold\r\nMultiplies (Mini LP): 1 on Oricon chart, 412,000 copies sold\r\nMultiplies (US version): 7 on Oricon chart, 186,000 copies sold\r\nBGM: 2 on Oricon chart, 275,000 copies sold\r\nTechnodelic: 4 on Oricon chart, 118,000 copies sold\r\nNaughty Boys: 1 on Oricon chart, 243,000 copies sold\r\nNaughty Boys Instrumental: 18 on Oricon chart, 31,000 copies sold\r\nService: 5 on Oricon chart, 135,000 copies sold\r\nAfter Service: 2 on Oricon chart, 123,000 copies sold\r\n(Source - booklet of the compilation \"We Love YMO\", 1998)","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:22061","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":67584,"name":"Pre YMO"},{"id":581920,"name":"Human Audio Sponge"},{"id":1149955,"name":"HASYMO"},{"id":3499205,"name":"Polyphonics (2)"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":5087,"name":"Ryuichi Sakamoto"},{"active":true,"id":19132,"name":"Haruomi Hosono"},{"active":true,"id":58981,"name":"Yukihiro Takahashi"}],"namevariations":["The Y.M.O.","The Yellow Magic Orchestra","Y M O","Y. M. O.","Y..M.O.","Y.M.O.","YMO","YMO (Yellow Magic Orchestra)","Yellow Magic","Yellow Man Orchestra","Ymoymo","Y̵M̵O̵","ymoymo","Йеллоу Мэджик Оркестра","イエロー・マジック・オーケストラ","黃色魔術交響樂團"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/22061-Yellow-Magic-Orchestra","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.ymo.org/","https://www.facebook.com/YMOofficial","https://www.sonymusic.co.jp/Music/Info/ymo/index_pc.html","https://myspace.com/hasymo","https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%A4%E3%82%A8%E3%83%AD%E3%83%BC%E3%83%BB%E3%83%9E%E3%82%B8%E3%83%83%E3%82%AF%E3%83%BB%E3%82%AA%E3%83%BC%E3%82%B1%E3%82%B9%E3%83%88%E3%83%A9","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_Magic_Orchestra","https://www.imdb.com/name/nm3576047/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2376076/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2376076","image":"https://i.discogs.com/Cov5o5z0d-nZj7mcMyMLOXWE3En2NuqMlsLlqEmUhDU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:400/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIzNzYw/NzYtMTQxMzQzMDc4/Ny02NjYyLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/aumFE-pz0Z6DZlAh9XpypmhE7vM5F8xJMnjBu1piMKU/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTIzNzYw/NzYtMTQxMzQzMDc4/Ny02NjYyLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Drum & Bass producer based in México City.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2376076","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":12145918,"name":"Guillermo Fernandez (8)"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2376076-Mukiyare","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.soundcloud.com/mukiyare","http://www.facebook.com/mukiyare.mx","http://www.mixcloud.com/mukiyare"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/419/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"419","image":"https://i.discogs.com/kUng52HIJYVCNlE7vyI9f0GCAMpsPK0Zhm7UPCDJSdc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:490/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQxOS0x/NTg5Mzk3MzUwLTY5/MTEuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/THHTZ0lWbQNdEQB8JSlo_Zqj9Ji8cG0zFdqdg7m9Fs8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQxOS0x/NTg5Mzk3MzUwLTY5/MTEuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"In 1990 David 'Man' McSherry and Steve Cobby began to record as Fila Brazillia. Hitherto their collaborations had been infrequent and ultra-spontaneous. Both had maintained positions in conventional bands but needed to trade the constraints of the \"write - rehearse - gig - record\" treadmill for a more fluent, and ultimately enjoyable approach. A nursery period for a music culled from sonic experiments and ideas quickly put to tape emerged. A treatment of all sounds as \"objet trouvé\" and a hobbyist attitude prevailed.\r\n\r\nWhen Dave Brennand a.k.a. [a=Porky (2)] heard a piece composed on a wet Wednesday, he asked to release it. They happily agreed. As previous unreleased work hadn't warranted anything but comedy monickers - \"Dada Black Sheep\" being one - a name was needed. At that time the media's \"killer dog frenzy\" was in full swing and a breed known as the fila brasiliero was the subject of a debate in the Commons. This was misheard on the radio by Steve, proposed and accepted for the single and eventually the name stuck. The track \"Mermaids\", was Fila Brazillia's first single, released in Spring 1991, and marked the beginning of a decade which saw Fila yield seven highly acclaimed albums and a skip-full of singles on Pork Recordings and over 60 remixes.\"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:419","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":9714,"name":"2 Loops Lautrec"}],"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":6191,"name":"Dave McSherry"},{"active":true,"id":62037,"name":"Steve Cobby"}],"namevariations":["FB","Fila Basilia","Fila Bazillia","Fila Brasilia","Fila Brazila","Fila Brazilia","Fila Brazilla","Fila Brazzilia","Fila Brizilia","Filia Brazillia","Filla Brazillia"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/419-Fila-Brazillia","type":"artist","urls":["http://web.archive.org/web/20200205014329/http://filabrazillia.net/","http://filabraz.bandcamp.com","http://www.facebook.com/FilaBrazillia","http://www.myspace.com/filabrazillia","http://www.myspace.com/filabrazilliafans","http://soundcloud.com/filabrazillia","http://twitter.com/FilaBrazillia","http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fila_Brazillia","http://www.youtube.com/user/filabrazillia1","http://www.youtube.com/user/FilaBrazilliaTV"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/4764773/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"4764773","image":"https://i.discogs.com/iNnjmLojiG7x5d2RMy18Dhi8RKnmVqrzpkPBXD8NkP8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ3NjQ3/NzMtMTU4NTQ5MjM5/OC02NDUzLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/iAiscKn1JoZMqo4OmgmyBp-Dtu9Cp0gF_fbVTAIE1wE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTQ3NjQ3/NzMtMTU4NTQ5MjM5/OC02NDUzLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"DJ/Producer from Mexico","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4764773","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["OMVVR"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4764773-Omaar","type":"artist","urls":["https://omaarmusic.bandcamp.com/","https://soundcloud.com/djomvvr","https://twitter.com/OMVVR","https://www.instagram.com/omaarsuaarez/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/5343938/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"5343938","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"Tina Pinnock, (born July 5, 1991) known professionally as HoodCelebrityy, is a Jamaican dancehall singer and songwriter from The Bronx, New York currently signed to Epic Records. She released two mixtapes in 2017, Can't Believe It's Just a Girl and Trap Vs. Reggae. The latter album peaked at number 9 on the Billboard Reggae Albums chart. Her 2017 single, \"Walking Trophy,\" peaked at number 22 on the R&B/Hip-Hop Airplay chart.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:5343938","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/5343938-Hoodcelebrityy","type":"artist","urls":["http://hoodcelebrityy.com/","https://soundcloud.com/hoodcelebrityy","https://www.instagram.com/hoodcelebrityy/","https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCgRyGg4DStCTALavIsGSNVQ","https://twitter.com/HoodCelebrityy"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/5515499/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"5515499","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:5515499","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":7363599,"name":"NYOKŌ BOKBAË"}],"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/5515499-Bamao-Yendé","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/6049826/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"6049826","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:6049826","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/6049826-Sanchez-Narvaez","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/artist/66261/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"i